<!--The story in this picture book is closer to otogi than kintei kyokasho though. Urashima only rides turtle on return.--><!--Japanese--><!--Do not link to Toyotama-hime. She is not actually called this in the old chronicles, plus, many sources prefer to designate her younger sister [[Tamayori-hime (mother of Jimmu)]] as "Oto-hime", since "oto" generally means second, cf. explanatory note (Miyao): --><!--乙姫は甲乙の乙であるので次女、二女、妹姫となります--><!--Thinking that opening the box might do some good, and (added in Kokutei 4)--><!--and touched his face (Kokutei 4)--><!--wrinkled and (kokutei 4)--><!--文部省--><!--日本書籍--><!--https://books.google.com/books?id=NnfhAAAAMAAJ--><!-- McKeon reads as "Ishihara Kazusaburo"--><!--: よく知られて口ずさまれるのは、やはり文語体--><!--Note: Keene's mistype "Shibuya Seiemon" should read "Shibukawa Seiemon", as he writes in note 3. The name Shibukawa Seiemon (渋川清右衛門) seems the correct one, but it can alternately be read "Kiyoemon", as Holmes's thesis has done.--><!--start of contribution by MartinPoulter, 10:07, 30 July 2015 --><!--end--><!--かたみの筥--><!--あひ構へてあけさせ給ふなと言ひけれども--><!--後--><!--吉川半七--><!--see {{nihongo||重箱|jūbako}}); not a three-drawered box--><!--仙(ひじり)の家の人なり--><!--Watadzumi, Wadatsumi--><!--{{Further|浦島太郎伝説関係資料}}--><!--ja:小島瓔礼--><!--岩崎美術社--><!--「与那覇村の人竜宮に遊ぶこと」--><!--、『[[中山道六十九次|木曾街道六十九次]]』。--><!--日本文學--><!--國文學: 解釈と敎材の硏究--><!--quotation=太郎の訪れた異郷が竜宮というのは御伽草子が初出である---><!--http://dl.ndl.go.jp/info:ndljp/pid/8099364 --><!--|quotation=The Ossian story.. is widespread and is even to be found among the best-known of the Japanese fairy-tales, 'Urashima Taro'.--><!--比較文化論叢：札幌大学文化学部紀要--><!--比較文化論叢：札幌大学文化学部紀要--><!--岩田書院--><!--横浜郷土史研究会--><!--横浜の史蹟と名勝--><!--あかね書房--><!--1959– --><!--明治大学教養論集--><!--東邦学誌--><!-- 比較民俗研究--><!--春風社--><!--大岡山書店--><!--沖繩文化論叢 2--><!--unattributed in the printed book--><!--[[:ja:長谷川武次郎]], 弘文社--><!--国際日本文学研究集会会議録--><!--苫小牧駒澤大学紀要--><!--苫小牧駒澤大学紀要--><!--苫小牧駒澤大学紀要--><!--成城大學經濟研究--><!--小林永濯 1843-1890--><!--彩流社--><!--4779113717, --><!--愛知淑徳大学論集一文学部・文学研究科篇-->